    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Verifies that nextIndex() and previousIndex() report the correct cursor position as the iterator navigates forward and backward through a 3-element list, including the wrap-around behaviour at both ends. Notation used in step comments: the element that would be returned by the next call to next() is enclosed in angle-brackets, e.g. [a] b c means the cursor sits before index 0, so nextIndex()==0 and previousIndex()==2 (the looped-back end of the list)."
   },
   {
    "id": "i2",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     30,
     31
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Initial state: cursor is before index 0 — [a] b c previousIndex wraps to the last index (2) because the iterator loops."
   },
   {
    "id": "i3",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     35,
     35
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Step forward: consume \"a\", cursor advances — a [b] c"
   },
   {
    "id": "i4",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     40,
     40
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Step backward: unconsume \"a\", cursor retreats — [a] b c"
   },
   {
    "id": "i5",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     45,
     47
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Step backward past the beginning: loops to the last element \"c\" — a b [c] previousIndex() returns 1 (index of \"b\") since \"c\" is at index 2 and calling previous() again would return \"b\"."
   },
   {
    "id": "i6",
